"1\n00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,529\nThe Learning Brain. Series 5: Belonging\n\n2\n00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:07,435\nEpisode 12\n\n3\n00:00:07,515 --> 00:00:09,653\nDesigning for belonging\n\n4\n00:00:12,453 --> 00:00:16,666\nAcross this series, we have seen that belonging is not a fixed trait.\n\n5\n00:00:17,197 --> 00:00:19,581\nIt is a question students keep asking,\n\n6\n00:00:19,620 --> 00:00:21,132\nand our courses answer it,\n\n7\n00:00:21,416 --> 00:00:23,076\noften without meaning to.\n\n8\n00:00:23,246 --> 00:00:24,919\nBefore a unit or a term.\n\n9\n00:00:25,359 --> 00:00:29,741\nCheck what the room and the materials say: who appears in your examples,\n\n10\n00:00:29,761 --> 00:00:31,132\nslides and readings.\n\n11\n00:00:31,569 --> 00:00:33,484\nPlan structure into class time.\n\n12\n00:00:33,891 --> 00:00:37,932\nAnd share the message that early struggle is common and temporary.\n\n13\n00:00:38,102 --> 00:00:38,727\nDuring.\n\n14\n00:00:38,732 --> 00:00:41,058\nUse active learning with clear structure.\n\n15\n00:00:41,580 --> 00:00:42,873\nGive wise feedback: high standards,\n\n16\n00:00:43,209 --> 00:00:46,626\nplus your belief that the student can reach them,\n\n17\n00:00:46,850 --> 00:00:48,486\nwith specific next steps.\n\n18\n00:00:48,870 --> 00:00:52,036\nShow a range of people students can see themselves in.\n\n19\n00:00:52,354 --> 00:00:55,062\nAnd talk about ability as something that grows,\n\n20\n00:00:55,082 --> 00:00:57,694\nin your words and in your course policies.\n\n21\n00:00:57,864 --> 00:00:59,449\nBefore high stakes moments,\n\n22\n00:00:59,469 --> 00:01:00,726\nlike a first exam,\n\n23\n00:01:00,932 --> 00:01:03,173\nconsider a brief values affirmation,\n\n24\n00:01:03,495 --> 00:01:06,716\nknowing that effects are small and vary by setting.\n\n25\n00:01:07,186 --> 00:01:09,923\nAnd present tests as a chance to show growth,\n\n26\n00:01:10,178 --> 00:01:11,737\nnot a verdict on a group.\n\n27\n00:01:11,907 --> 00:01:12,577\nAfter.\n\n28\n00:01:12,579 --> 00:01:14,277\nLook at outcomes by group,\n\n29\n00:01:14,297 --> 00:01:15,622\nnot just averages.\n\n30\n00:01:15,945 --> 00:01:18,041\nRead feedback for signs of doubt.\n\n31\n00:01:18,458 --> 00:01:22,375\nAnd for first generation students,\n\n32\n00:01:22,717 --> 00:01:23,845\nspell out the unwritten rules.\n\n33\n00:01:24,258 --> 00:01:27,351\nThen close the loop: tell students what you changed because of their feedback.\n\n34\n00:01:27,521 --> 00:01:28,534\nSome caution.\n\n35\n00:01:28,853 --> 00:01:30,854\nMany of these effects are modest,\n\n36\n00:01:30,874 --> 00:01:32,679\nand some depend on context.\n\n37\n00:01:33,020 --> 00:01:34,988\nNo single fix works alone.\n\n38\n00:01:35,282 --> 00:01:36,868\nThe aim is many small,\n\n39\n00:01:36,888 --> 00:01:38,350\nconsistent signals.\n\n40\n00:01:38,520 --> 00:01:39,322\nFor teaching.\n\n41\n00:01:39,683 --> 00:01:41,336\nPick one change for before,\n\n42\n00:01:41,426 --> 00:01:44,403\none for during, and one for after your next unit.\n\n43\n00:01:44,856 --> 00:01:46,426\nThen check whether it worked.\n\n44\n00:01:46,809 --> 00:01:51,476\nOne tip to share with students: take one small belonging step each week,\n\n45\n00:01:51,663 --> 00:01:55,189\nlike visiting office hours or joining a study group.\n\n46\n00:01:55,359 --> 00:01:57,561\nBelonging is built in small moments.\n\n47\n00:01:57,786 --> 00:01:59,392\nDesign them on purpose.\n\n48\n00:01:59,655 --> 00:02:01,711\nThanks for watching series five.\n\n"
